<description>&lt;p&gt;Ethiopian forces have captured Gual Gemahalo near Badme and are fighting Eritrean-backed fighters while shelling Alamata, and Somali militants attacked an Ethiopian base killing 43 soldiers. Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed warned Eritrea to stop supporting Ethiopia's enemies and announced the resumption of Ethiopian Airlines flights to Aksum and the escort of 300 Kenyan trucks across Moyale after a ceasefire. Eritrea has accused Ethiopia of using Red Sea diplomacy to advance territorial ambitions and the war in Amhara is threatening water security in the Nile Basin. A machine-learning analysis shows sharp geographic divides in Ethiopian digital activism.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxPaURqMks0ZUxKX2lrYXNvdjI2WjJKRkNGcWlnX29janhtVTMtTGhlMmFIMDliNmxhY2dXUWcyRkZPT0Zrek9fLWdhQ1VtWHNydktjd1liR1A3NjJMZjhvQkcxU1dMVUsxTi0zUmxIWF9qZURFWGhXUGY5TWxuMmlqYlBqZFZuamh2X0NOc3hlTldnSU9vcEtrWENRcWZ1X053SFpMbE1NQk5VQS1PdEc1N3VEaGJkQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Borkena&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZ0FVX3lxTE44QlNjM3JaMlY5c3BXV2YzTEN2SHl1Tk5rMmV4bTFQREg4a1VIeVEzQ3FxTzZwR1p6QUFCRG9nOXpfckM2QTJiVENLSGhqVkg3WUxRTGFsT3ZUUmZqLVU2Tmo0b0FMeXc?oc=5&quot;&gt;DNE Africa&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifEFVX3lxTFBXU2czU2V2RHNXalVEZkROTFdSS09lcDhFQlBQSG5jWmxjeF9hZUhjMHNoTUt3N0plT2N4Q0tlSll3MV9zU1l6aE04eW1LWlhfWEVLa2Zac1I2ekJmMWRFMWFmQ0UzRHRvSERuNGFuc2hfYmw2YW9YQXFNdkY?oc=5&quot;&gt;kulu-media.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxNZHFvZ0NYUE9DXzdlVXNhSl9SZ1JreUdCTGppc2t1YWl2SUtQYlljY3JqeXdteEF6YVpKNWVtV3FJRjMxazc4b3VoTVBGLUE4azVPbHBCSlFua3NFM1Z0UGxzZnI5OGNOT3hIWHU3akR0d201NGw2ckxPX0tPamY0SzV4VXdTZ1MwRENCejNvcDRKaDZMdGhUcUx3RVpwWXRuRHpCYzJpYUpuTFYtSHAxUGFsSHRvQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;The EastAfrican&lt;/a&g